\
Mother, why do ^\'92\uc0\u9632 ou think of dying and torture \
yourself ? Take pity on me, your child. J am a beggar. \
Look here, my guru was a great saint and highly merciful. \
I fatigued myself in trying to serve him and yet he did \
not utter any mantra in my ear. Instead, he first shaved \
me clean and then begged of me, two pice. What he \
wanted was not metallic coin \'97 he did not care even for \
gold, but only Nishta and Sahuri i.e., faith and courage- \
ous patience. I gave these to him at once and he w^as \
pleased. \
\
Mother, Saburi is courage, do not discard it. It \
ferries you across to the distant goal. It gives manli- \
ness to men, eradicates sin and dejection and overcomes \
all fear. \
\
For 12 years I waited on my Guru, who is peerless and \
loving. How can I describe his love to me ? When he was \
Dhyanasta (in love-trance) I sat and gazed at him ; and we \
were both filled with Bliss. I cared not to turn my eye \
